Package: enviroplus-exporter
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends},
 python3 (>= 3.11),
 python3-libgpiod (>= 2.1.3),
 python3-smbus2,
 python3-serial,
 python3-prometheus-client
Description: Prometheus exporter for the Pimoroni Enviro+ sensor board
 Exposes the BME280 (temperature, pressure, humidity), LTR559 (light, proximity),
 MICS6814 (gas) and PMS5003 (particulates) readings on an HTTP port for Prometheus.
 .
 A lean fork of tijmenvandenbrink/enviroplus_exporter: InfluxDB and Luftdaten
 posting are removed, and the Pimoroni libraries it needs are bundled in a private
 directory (/usr/lib/enviroplus), so no virtualenv, pip, numpy or build tools are needed.

Package: enviroplus-lcd
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends},
 enviroplus-exporter (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3 (>= 3.11),
 python3-numpy,
 python3-pil,
 python3-spidev,
 fonts-roboto-unhinted
Description: Clock display for the Pimoroni Enviro+ 0.96" LCD
 Shows the host name and time on the Enviro+ ST7735 display. Optional: it pulls
 in numpy and Pillow, which the exporter itself does not need. The unit only
 starts when /dev/spidev0.1 exists, so the SPI interface (dtparam=spi=on in
 /boot/firmware/config.txt) must be enabled.
